editor.nod_help.guide.create.symbols=Optionally add <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a> for symbols left or right of values.
editor.nod_help.guide.create.rules=Write the conversion with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> or <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a>.
editor.nod_help.guide.create.validate=Use <b>Validate</b> to find syntax errors and <b>Test</b> to try the result.
editor.nod_help.guide.create.save=Save the file when the converter is correct.
editor.nod_help.guide.tips_title=Command tips
editor.nod_help.guide.tips=The blue balloon gives short help for the line where the caret is placed. Sometimes it also shows a more modern form. Use <b>Replace</b> only when you really want that modern form; <b>More help</b> opens the full command page.
editor.nod_help.guide.undo_title=Undo, redo and restore
editor.nod_help.guide.undo=<b>Undo</b> and <b>Redo</b> are about recent text edits. <b>Restore</b> is larger: it returns the current tab to the last opened or saved version. <b>Tools &gt; Repair lines</b> is different; it tries to repair pasted or merged NOD lines.
editor.nod_help.full.classic_book=<h2>Why old and new live together</h2><p>Syscalculator 2.0 is not a break with old NOD files. The goal is that older converters remain recognizable, while the editor gives more help while writing, testing and maintaining them.</p><h2>What made classic NOD strong</h2><p>Classic NOD was small and direct. A <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> line calculated further with <code>ans</code>. A <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> line translated a fixed value. A <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> line changed the start of text, for example in old phone renumbering files.</p><h2>What NOD 2.0 adds</h2><p>NOD 2.0 keeps that simple base, but surrounds it with a modern editor: syntax coloring, command tips, right-click help, templates, validation, test output, preview and restore. The language stays readable, while the environment helps find mistakes faster.</p><h2>Overview</h2><table><tr><th>Syscalculator 1.73 / NOD 1.x</th><th>Syscalculator 2.0 / NOD editor</th></tr><tr><td>Small text files with classic commands such as <code>Name</code>, <code>input1</code>, <code>input2</code>, <code>math</code>, <code>trans</code>, <code>chg</code> and <code>end</code>.</td><td>The same base still works, so older NOD files remain recognizable and usable.</td></tr><tr><td>You often had to remember where symbols appeared and then test in the old calculator.</td><td>The editor shows a live preview/simulator where <code>Symb1</code> through <code>Symb4</code> are immediately visible.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg</code> was mainly classic prefix replacement, useful for old phone renumbering.</td><td><code>chg</code> stays compatible, but NOD 2.0 can also use patterns with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td>Help mostly came from examples and experience.</td><td>The editor has suggestions, right-click help, command pages and examples by NOD type.</td></tr></table><h2>Rule of thumb</h2><p>Use old commands when maintaining an existing file. Use the modern form when the editor suggests it and the file becomes clearer. Compatibility matters, but readability is the goal.</p>
editor.nod_help.full.structure=<h2>Basic structure</h2><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;URLN Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format ##.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre>
editor.nod_help.full.workflow=<h2>Workflow</h2><ol><li>Start with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, and <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a>; then the converter has a name and visible labels.</li><li>Optionally choose symbols with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a>. Use left or right per value, not both.</li><li>Add conversion rules: <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> for calculations, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> for exact text translation, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> for prefix changes.</li><li>Use <b>Validate</b> or F5 to check syntax and <b>Test</b> or F6 to see the result.</li><li>Place <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> at the end.</li></ol>
editor.nod_help.full.symbols=<h2>Symbols</h2><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>Position</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Symb1</td><td>left of input</td><td>DM 25</td></tr><tr><td>Symb2</td><td>left of output</td><td>EUR 25</td></tr><tr><td>Symb3</td><td>right of input</td><td>25 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Symb4</td><td>right of output</td><td>25 lb</td></tr></table><p>Usually choose left or right per value, not both, to avoid duplicate text such as <code>DM 25 DM</code>.</p>
editor.nod_help.full.commands=<h2>Important commands</h2><ul><li><b>math</b>: calculates with <code>ans</code>.</li><li><b>trans</b>: translates exact text values.</li><li><b>chg</b>: changes starting text/prefix; also supports <code>x</code> patterns such as <code>050-2xxxxx</code>, with the most specific prefix winning.</li><li><b>indoprint ... indoend</b>: introduction text block. Do not forget <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoend"><code>indoend</code></a>.</li><li><b>end</b>: closes the NOD file.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.full.examples=<h2>Examples by NOD type</h2><p>NOD files can describe different kinds of converters. Choose the pattern that fits what you want to build.</p><h3>1. Calculation tool with math</h3><p>Use this for numbers: temperature, distance, weight, currency, percentage.</p><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format ##.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre><h3>2. Translation tool with trans</h3><p>Use this when the full input must exactly match a known value. Separate old and new with a comma. Use quotes when values contain spaces or commas.</p><pre>Name Postcode to address demo&#13;&#10;input1 Postcode house number&#13;&#10;input2 Address&#13;&#10;trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"&#13;&#10;end</pre><h3>3. Prefix/pattern tool with chg</h3><p>Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> when only the start of the text changes. Separate old and new with a comma. <code>x</code> patterns are allowed, useful for old phone renumbering tables.</p><pre>Name Operation Decibel example&#13;&#10;input1 Old phone number&#13;&#10;input2 New phone number&#13;&#10;chg "01751-xxxxx","070-51xxxxx"&#13;&#10;chg "050-2xxxxx","050-52xxxxx"&#13;&#10;end</pre><h3>4. Tool with left/right symbols</h3><p>Use symbols to display values neatly. Choose left or right per value.</p><pre>Name German mark to euro&#13;&#10;input1 Mark&#13;&#10;input2 Euro&#13;&#10;Symb1 DM&#13;&#10;Symb2 EUR&#13;&#10;format ##.00&#13;&#10;math ans / 1.95583&#13;&#10;end</pre><h3>5. Introduction text with indoprint</h3><p>Use this when the user should see instructions before using the converter.</p><pre>indoprint This converter changes Celsius to Fahrenheit.&#13;&#10;indoprint Enter a temperature in degrees Celsius.&#13;&#10;indoend</pre><h3>6. Equation solving with equation</h3><p>Use this for formula-like problems where an unknown variable should be solved.</p><pre>Name Solve equation&#13;&#10;given y = 20&#13;&#10;equation y = x * 2&#13;&#10;solve x&#13;&#10;constraint x >= 0&#13;&#10;end</pre><h3>7. Example as shown in the window</h3><p>This shows where labels, input, result, and symbols appear on screen.</p><div class="dialog-example"><div class="dialog-title">EuroCalculator</div><div class="dialog-menu"><span>File</span><span>Edit</span><span>Config</span><span>Tools</span><span>About</span></div><div class="dialog-body"><div class="dialog-row"><span></span><div class="dialog-label">Value in Deutsch Mark</div><span></span></div><div class="dialog-row"><span class="dialog-radio on"></span><div class="dialog-input">22</div><div class="dialog-symbol">DM</div></div><div class="dialog-row"><span></span><div class="dialog-label">Value in euros</div><span></span></div><div class="dialog-row"><span class="dialog-radio"></span><div class="dialog-input">11.25</div><span></span></div><div class="dialog-options"><span>&#9633; Digit group</span><span>&#9745; Decimals</span><span>2</span></div></div></div><pre>Name German mark to euro&#13;&#10;input1 Value in Deutsch Mark&#13;&#10;input2 Value in euros&#13;&#10;Symb3 DM&#13;&#10;format ##.00&#13;&#10;math ans / 1.95583&#13;&#10;end</pre>
editor.nod_help.full.troubleshooting=<h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li><b>Duplicate symbols:</b> do not use both left and right symbols for the same value, otherwise you can get text such as <code>DM 25 DM</code>.</li><li><b>Introduction without end:</b> close every <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoprint"><code>indoprint</code></a> block with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoend"><code>indoend</code></a>.</li><li><b>Math without ans:</b> use <code>ans</code> as the current value, for example <code>math ans * 100</code>.</li><li><b>No end:</b> place <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> at the end of the file.</li><li><b>Comma/dot:</b> decimals often work with comma or dot; always test with F6.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.name=<div class="title">Name</div><div class="syntax">Name Celsius to Fahrenheit</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> internal converter name.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>Name Postcode to address demo</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.urln=<div class="title">URLN</div><div class="syntax">URLN User title</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> visible title or description for the user.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>URLN Phone renumbering 1995 complete</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.input1=<div class="title">input1</div><div class="syntax">input1 Celsius</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> label of the input value.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>input1 Old phone number</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.input2=<div class="title">input2</div><div class="syntax">input2 Fahrenheit</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> label of the output value.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>input2 New phone number</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.symb1=<div class="title">Symb1</div><div class="syntax">Symb1 DM</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> symbol left of input1.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>Symb1 DM</code> displays <code>DM 25</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.symb2=<div class="title">Symb2</div><div class="syntax">Symb2 EUR</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> symbol left of input2/output.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>Symb2 EUR</code> displays <code>EUR 12.78</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.symb3=<div class="title">Symb3</div><div class="syntax">Symb3 kg</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> symbol right of input1.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>Symb3 kg</code> displays <code>25 kg</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.symb4=<div class="title">Symb4</div><div class="syntax">Symb4 lb</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> symbol right of input2/output.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>Symb4 lb</code> displays <code>55 lb</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.format=<div class="title">format</div><div class="syntax">format ##.00</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> controls how many decimals the result shows.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>format ##.00</code> displays <code>12.50</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.mode=<div class="title">mode</div><div class="syntax">mode calculator</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> extra setting for converter type.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>mode calculator</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.math=<div class="title">math</div><div class="syntax">math ans * 1.8</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> runs a calculation step with <code>ans</code> as current value.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>math ans + 32</code> adds 32 to the current value.</div>
editor.nod_help.chg=<div class="title">chg</div><div class="syntax">chg "old-prefix","new-prefix"</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> changes the start of text, for example codes or phone numbers.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>chg "01751-xxxxx","070-51xxxxx"</code> turns <code>01751-12345</code> into <code>070-5112345</code>.</div><div><b>Patterns:</b> <code>x</code> may mark the remaining digits. If multiple rules match, the longest/most specific prefix wins.</div>
editor.nod_help.trans=<div class="title">trans</div><div class="syntax">trans "old value","new value"</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> translates a complete value. NOD 1.0 matches exactly; NOD 2.0 can then match smarter compact text.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>trans "dank je","thank you"</code> also translates input such as <code>dank_je</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.trans.improved=<h2>Improved trans: smarter than NOD 1.0</h2><div class="notice improved"><b>Compatible:</b> classic NOD 1.0 <code>trans</code> still tries exact matches first. NOD 2.0 only then tries a smart compact match.</div><table class="syntax-compare"><tr><th>Behavior</th><th>NOD 1.0</th><th>NOD 2.0</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Exact value</td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><code>trans "hallo","hello"</code></td></tr><tr><td>Ignore letter case</td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><code>Hallo</code> matches <code>hallo</code></td></tr><tr><td>Ignore spaces, dots, dashes and underscore</td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><code>dank_je</code>, <code>dank je</code> and <code>dank-je</code> can hit the same trans rule</td></tr><tr><td>Ambiguous smart match</td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>When two compact matches exist, it does not silently translate wrongly; the input stays unchanged.</td></tr></table><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>NOD 1.0: classic exact</h3><pre>Name Classic trans&#13;&#10;input1 Dutch&#13;&#10;input2 English&#13;&#10;trans "hallo","hello"&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Made for fixed values. Exact rules still have priority.</p></div><div class="example-card"><h3>NOD 2.0: improved trans</h3><pre>Name Smart trans&#13;&#10;input1 Dutch&#13;&#10;input2 English&#13;&#10;trans "dank je","thank you"&#13;&#10;trans "goedemorgen","good morning"&#13;&#10;end</pre><p><code>dank_je</code>, <code>DANK-JE</code> and <code>dank je</code> can all return <code>thank you</code>.</p></div></div><p><b>Rule of thumb:</b> use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> for complete values. Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> when only the beginning or a pattern changes.</p>
editor.nod_help.reverse=<div class="title">reverse</div><div class="syntax">reverse ans / 1.8</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> manual reverse calculation rule.</div><div><b>Example:</b> with <code>math ans * 1.8</code>, use <code>reverse ans / 1.8</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.field=<div class="title">field</div><div class="syntax">field ColumnName</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> starts a data field definition.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>field Phone</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.table=<div class="title">table</div><div class="syntax">table TableName</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> name of the source table.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>table Customers</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.output=<div class="title">output</div><div class="syntax">output ResultColumn</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> name of the output field.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>output PhoneNew</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.phoneformat=<div class="title">phoneformat</div><div class="syntax">phoneformat country NL</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> normalizes phone numbers inside a <code>field</code> block in <code>mode data</code>.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>phoneformat remove_spaces true</code> removes spaces; <code>phoneformat normalize_international true</code> normalizes Dutch international notation.</div>
editor.nod_help.lookup=<div class="title">lookup</div><div class="syntax">lookup Countries</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> starts a lookup definition.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>lookup Countries</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.match=<div class="title">match</div><div class="syntax">match code = NL</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> describes how a lookup is matched.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>match postcode = 2566GB</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.given=<div class="title">given</div><div class="syntax">given x = 10</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> known value for an equation.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>given y = 20</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.equation=<div class="title">equation</div><div class="syntax">equation y = x * 2</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> defines an equation.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>equation y = x * 2</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.solve=<div class="title">solve</div><div class="syntax">solve x</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> tells which variable should be solved.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>solve x</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.constraint=<div class="title">constraint</div><div class="syntax">constraint x >= 0</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> condition for a solution.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>constraint x >= 0</code> prevents negative solutions.</div>
editor.nod_help.preview=<div class="title">preview</div><div class="syntax">preview Example text</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> text for preview/sample display.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>preview Enter 2566 GB 241</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.backup=<div class="title">backup</div><div class="syntax">backup true</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> compatibility setting from older NOD files.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>backup true</code>.</div>
editor.nod_help.indoprint=<div class="title">indoprint</div><div class="syntax">indoprint Introduction text</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> line of introduction text shown before use.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>indoprint This converter uses the Decibel table.</code> Then close with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoend"><code>indoend</code></a>.</div>
editor.nod_help.indoend=<div class="title">indoend</div><div class="syntax">indoend</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> end of an introduction text block.</div><div><b>Example:</b> <code>indoprint Help text</code> followed by <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoend"><code>indoend</code></a>.</div>
editor.nod_help.end=<div class="title">end</div><div class="syntax">end</div><div><b>Meaning:</b> end of the NOD file.</div><div><b>Example:</b> place <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> as the last line.</div>
editor.nod_insert.indoprint=indoprint Introduction text\nindoend

editor.nod_help.chg.extra=<h2>chg examples</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> changes the beginning of text. It is useful for phone numbers, codes, prefixes, and old renumbering tables.</p><div class="notice"><b>Structure:</b> left is what to find, right is the new form. Use quotes when values contain spaces, commas, or special characters.</div><details open><summary>Replace a prefix</summary><table><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Rule</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Old prefix to new</td><td><code>chg "01751","07051"</code></td><td><code>0175112345</code> becomes <code>0705112345</code></td></tr><tr><td>With dash</td><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><code>01751-12345</code> becomes <code>070-5112345</code></td></tr><tr><td>Longest match wins</td><td>put specific rules above broad rules</td><td><code>01751-9xxxx</code> can be handled separately</td></tr></table><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: The Hague 070</h3><pre>Name Renumbering The Hague&#13;&#10;input1 Old phone number&#13;&#10;input2 New phone number&#13;&#10;chg "01751-xxxxx","070-51xxxxx"&#13;&#10;chg "01750-xxxxx","070-50xxxxx"&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: item code</h3><pre>Name Update item code&#13;&#10;input1 Old code&#13;&#10;input2 New code&#13;&#10;chg "OLD-","NEW-"&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details><details><summary>Pattern with x</summary><p>Use <code>x</code> for characters that must be kept. This is useful for old phone renumbering tables.</p><pre>chg "050-2xxxxx","050-52xxxxx"</pre><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: pattern rule</h3><pre>Name Phone pattern&#13;&#10;input1 Old&#13;&#10;input2 New&#13;&#10;chg "050-2xxxxx","050-52xxxxx"&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details><details><summary>Common chg mistakes</summary><ul><li>Putting a broad rule above a specific rule.</li><li>Forgetting the comma between old and new.</li><li>Using spaces or commas without quotes.</li><li>Using <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> when you need an exact full-value translation; then use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.math.extra=<h2>Math at a glance</h2>&#13;&#10;<p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> calculates with <code>ans</code>. On the first line <code>ans</code> is the input value; on following lines it is the previous result.</p>&#13;&#10;<div class="notice"><b>Structure:</b> choose the calculation type first, then write the matching syntax. For larger formulas, use parentheses or multiple lines.</div>&#13;&#10;<div class="math-flow"><span class="math-pill">1. Basic</span><span class="math-pill">2. Functions</span><span class="math-pill">3. Complex formula</span><span class="math-pill">4. Reverse or calculus</span></div>&#13;&#10;<h2>Syntax by group</h2>&#13;&#10;<details open><summary>Basic operations</summary><table><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Add</td><td><code>math ans + number</code></td><td><code>math ans + 32</code></td></tr><tr><td>Subtract</td><td><code>math ans - number</code></td><td><code>math ans - 10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Multiply</td><td><code>math ans * factor</code></td><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td></tr><tr><td>Divide</td><td><code>math ans / factor</code></td><td><code>math ans / 1.95583</code></td></tr></table><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: euro to cents</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mtext>cents</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>euro</mtext><mo>&#x00D7;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Euro to cents&#13;&#10;input1 Euro&#13;&#10;input2 Cents&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 100&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: discount</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mtext>new</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>price</mtext><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Price minus discount&#13;&#10;input1 Price&#13;&#10;input2 After 10 discount&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans - 10&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Functions and constants</summary><table><tr><th>Group</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td><code>math ans^2</code> or <code>math pow(ans,3)</code></td><td>Square, cube, and more.</td></tr><tr><td>Square root</td><td><code>math sqrt(ans)</code></td><td>Also usable inside larger formulas.</td></tr><tr><td>Pi and e</td><td><code>math pi * ans^2</code><br><code>math e^ans</code></td><td>Circle and exponential examples.</td></tr><tr><td>Logarithm</td><td><code>math log(ans)</code><br><code>math log(ans,2)</code><br><code>math ln(ans)</code></td><td><code>log(ans)</code> is log10.</td></tr><tr><td>Degrees</td><td><code>math sind(ans)</code><br><code>math cosd(ans)</code><br><code>math tand(ans)</code></td><td>Use <code>sin/cos/tan</code> for radians.</td></tr><tr><td>Modulo</td><td><code>math mod(ans,2)</code><br><code>math ans % 5</code></td><td>Remainders, even/odd tests.</td></tr></table><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: circle</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#x03C0;</mi><mo>&#x00B7;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Circle area&#13;&#10;input1 Radius&#13;&#10;input2 Area&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math pi * ans^2&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: log base 2</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><msub><mo>log</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Log base 2&#13;&#10;input1 Number&#13;&#10;input2 Log2&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math log(ans,2)&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Complex expressions</summary><p>Use parentheses when order matters. Always write multiplication explicitly with <code>*</code>.</p><pre>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;math ((ans + 10) * 2) / 3&#13;&#10;math ans * (1 + 0.04)^5</pre><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: parentheses</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#x00D7;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></div><pre>Name Parentheses example&#13;&#10;input1 Value&#13;&#10;input2 Result&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ((ans + 10) * 2) / 3&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: interest</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mtext>value</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>start</mtext><mo>&#x00D7;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Interest 5 years&#13;&#10;input1 Start amount&#13;&#10;input2 Value&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * (1 + 0.04)^5&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: Pythagoras</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Hypotenuse&#13;&#10;input1 Side a&#13;&#10;input2 Side c&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Here <code>ans</code> is side <code>a</code>. The other side is fixed at <code>5</code>.</p></div></div></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Calculus: diff, integral, limit</summary><table><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Derivative</td><td><code>math diff ans^2</code></td><td>Approximates the slope at the input value.</td></tr><tr><td>Integral</td><td><code>math integral 0,1 ans^2</code></td><td>Approximates area from 0 to 1.</td></tr><tr><td>Limit</td><td><code>math limit 0 sin(ans)/ans</code></td><td>Approximates the limit around 0.</td></tr></table><div class="notice"><b>Important:</b> calculus is numeric. It gives an approximation, not symbolic CAS output.</div><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: limit</h3><pre>Name Sine limit&#13;&#10;input1 x&#13;&#10;input2 Limit&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math limit 0 sin(ans)/ans&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: derivative</h3><pre>Name Square derivative&#13;&#10;input1 x&#13;&#10;input2 Slope&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math diff ans^2&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: integral</h3><pre>Name Square integral&#13;&#10;input1 x&#13;&#10;input2 Area&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math integral 0,1 ans^2&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details>&#13;&#10;<h2>Common math mistakes</h2><ul><li>Forgetting <code>ans</code>: write <code>math ans * 100</code>, not <code>math * 100</code>.</li><li>Putting too much into one line when steps would be clearer.</li><li>Using <code>sin</code> when you mean degrees. Use <code>sind</code>.</li><li>Expecting reverse conversion for a complex formula without <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a>.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.trans.extra=<h2>trans examples</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> translates a complete value. It is meant for words, fixed codes, statuses, postcodes, or short lists.</p><div class="notice"><b>Structure:</b> <code>trans "old value","new value"</code>. The complete input must match the left value.</div><details open><summary>Translate exact text</summary><table><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Rule</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td>Translate word</td><td><code>trans "hallo","hello"</code></td><td><code>hallo</code> becomes <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td>Translate status</td><td><code>trans "open","in progress"</code></td><td><code>open</code> becomes <code>in progress</code></td></tr><tr><td>Address lookup</td><td><code>trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"</code></td><td>postcode + house number becomes address</td></tr></table><div class="example-grid"><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: Dutch to English</h3><pre>Name Dutch English demo&#13;&#10;input1 Dutch&#13;&#10;input2 English&#13;&#10;trans "hallo","hello"&#13;&#10;trans "dank je","thank you"&#13;&#10;trans "goedemorgen","good morning"&#13;&#10;end</pre></div><div class="example-card"><h3>Example: postcode demo</h3><pre>Name Postcode to address demo&#13;&#10;input1 Postcode house number&#13;&#10;input2 Address&#13;&#10;trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"&#13;&#10;end</pre></div></div></details><details><summary>When trans, when chg?</summary><table><tr><th>Use</th><th>When</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a></td><td>the entire input is known exactly</td><td><code>hallo</code> to <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td><td>only the beginning or pattern changes</td><td><code>01751-xxxxx</code> to <code>070-51xxxxx</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Common trans mistakes</summary><ul><li>Reversing direction: left is input, right is output.</li><li>Expecting a partial match. Use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> for that.</li><li>Using a comma in a value without quotes.</li><li>Creating duplicate translations for the same input.</li></ul></details>

editor.nod_help.mode.extra=<h2>When do you use mode?</h2>&#13;&#10;<p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> tells what kind of NOD file you are making. For normal conversion tools, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> is usually not needed; without mode it works as a normal converter.</p>&#13;&#10;<div class="notice"><b>Rule of thumb:</b> use <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> only when the file has a special type, such as data processing or equation solving.</div>&#13;&#10;<details open><summary>Common modes</summary><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Use</th><th>Important commands</th></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td>Normal converter or calculation helper.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td>Process rows or fields in a table.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:phoneformat"><code>phoneformat</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td>Solve an equation.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:constraint"><code>constraint</code></a></td></tr></table></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Example: normal converter</summary><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Here <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> is not required. This is the default.</p></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Example: data processing</summary><pre>Name Clean customer phones&#13;&#10;mode data&#13;&#10;table customers&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;field phone&#13;&#10;phoneformat country NL&#13;&#10;chg "01751-xxxxx","070-51xxxxx"&#13;&#10;output phone_new&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Use <code>mode data</code> when the NOD file processes table fields.</p></details>&#13;&#10;<details><summary>Example: equation solving</summary><pre>Name Solve equation&#13;&#10;mode equation&#13;&#10;given y = 20&#13;&#10;equation y = x * 2&#13;&#10;solve x&#13;&#10;constraint x >= 0&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Use <code>mode equation</code> when you want to solve an unknown variable.</p></details>
editor.nod_help.full.classic=<h2>NOD editor introduction</h2><p>The NOD editor is the workspace for converters. Write code at the top, test input and output below, and use the live preview/simulator on the right to see labels, symbols, introduction text and results.</p><h2>Classic 1.73 versus NOD 2.0</h2><table><tr><th>Syscalculator 1.73 / NOD 1.0</th><th>Syscalculator 2.0 / NOD editor</th></tr><tr><td>Classic text files with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> and <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a>.</td><td>The same base still works, so older NOD files remain recognizable.</td></tr><tr><td>You often had to remember where symbols appeared and test in the old calculator.</td><td>The preview immediately shows <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a> left or right of the values.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> was classic prefix replacement, useful for old phone renumbering.</td><td>Old <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> stays compatible; NOD 2.0 adds pattern rules with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td>Help mostly came from examples and experience.</td><td>The editor has suggestions, right-click help, multiple help pages and examples by NOD type.</td></tr></table><h2>Syntax: full NOD 1.0 and NOD 2.0 overview</h2><p>This table shows which syntax comes from classic NOD files and what was added in NOD 2.0.</p><table class="syntax-compare"><tr><th>Syntax / feature</th><th>NOD 1.0</th><th>NOD 2.0</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Converter name/title.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:urln"><code>URLN</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Reference/source line remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Labels for input and output.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:result"><code>Result</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:resfou"><code>Resfou</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Result label and error text.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Symbols left/right of input and output; NOD 2.0 shows them in preview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>format #.00</code></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Number formatting stays the same.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 uses <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> for special file types; normal converters also work without mode.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>For table/field processing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>For solving equations with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Classic calculation with <code>ans</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)</code></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Richer formulas and functions in NOD 2.0.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Classic prefix replacement keeps working.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</code></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>New in NOD 2.0: pattern with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td><code>trans "old","new"</code></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Exact text translation remains compatible.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Reverse direction of a converter.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 data converters with fields and output construction.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:phoneformat"><code>phoneformat</code></a></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Format phone numbers in data/number converters.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:lookup"><code>lookup</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:match"><code>match</code></a></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Look up tables or connect values.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:constraint"><code>constraint</code></a></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Solve equations with constraints.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:preview"><code>preview</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:backup"><code>backup</code></a></td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Editor/safety information for NOD 2.0 files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>indoprint ... indoend</code></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Introduction text remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>Closes the NOD file.</td></tr><tr><td>Live preview, suggestions, right-click help</td><td><span class="no">&#10005;</span></td><td><span class="yes">&#10003;</span></td><td>This is editor help, not old runtime syntax.</td></tr></table><h2>What stays the same?</h2><ul><li>Commands are still line-based and readable.</li><li><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> closes the file.</li><li>A simple converter remains short: name, labels, format and a few rules.</li></ul><h2>What is new?</h2><ul><li>Live preview and converter simulator.</li><li>Graph 2D for math-converter graphs.</li><li>Suggestions while typing.</li><li>Richer help per command.</li><li>More examples for <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a>, symbols and <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoprint"><code>indoprint</code></a>.</li></ul>
