legal.license.title=License Agreement
legal.license.intro=This license agreement applies to Syscalculator 2.0, published by Edward Tie / Tiedragon.
legal.license.scope.title=Scope
legal.license.scope.body=Syscalculator is licensed software. The daily and beta builds are evaluation builds and may be changed, replaced or withdrawn during development.
legal.license.daily.title=Daily and Beta Builds
legal.license.daily.body=Daily and beta builds are provided for testing, feedback and evaluation. They may contain unfinished features, regressions or diagnostic behavior.
legal.license.use.title=Permitted Use
legal.license.use.personal=You may install and use Syscalculator for personal work, testing and learning.
legal.license.use.internal=Organizations may evaluate Syscalculator internally unless a separate written agreement says otherwise.
legal.license.use.no_resale=You may not sell, rent, sublicense or redistribute Syscalculator as your own product.
legal.license.ownership.title=Ownership
legal.license.ownership.body=Syscalculator, the Tiedragon name, application code, graph modules, help content and related assets remain the property of Edward Tie / Tiedragon unless a file explicitly states another license.
legal.license.warranty.title=No Warranty
legal.license.warranty.body=Syscalculator is provided as-is. Calculations, conversions and generated output should be checked by the user before being used for important decisions.
legal.license.liability.title=Limitation of Liability
legal.license.liability.body=To the maximum extent allowed by law, Tiedragon is not liable for indirect damage, data loss, business interruption or decisions made from unchecked output.
legal.license.third_party.title=Third-Party Components
legal.license.third_party.body=Syscalculator may use third-party components such as .NET, WebView2, GitHub distribution services or Microsoft platform components. Those components remain subject to their own terms.
legal.license.contact.title=Contact
legal.license.contact.body=Questions about licensing can be sent to info@tiedragon.com.
legal.privacy.title=Privacy Statement
legal.privacy.intro=This privacy statement applies to Syscalculator, published by Edward Tie / Tiedragon.
legal.privacy.summary.title=Short Summary
legal.privacy.summary.body=Syscalculator is a desktop application. Calculations, conversions, NOD files and settings are normally processed locally on your computer. Syscalculator does not sell personal data and does not use advertising or analytics tracking.
legal.privacy.local.title=Local Data
legal.privacy.local.body=Syscalculator may store local data needed to use the application.
legal.privacy.local.settings=Application settings.
legal.privacy.local.language=Selected language and update channel.
legal.privacy.local.recent=Recent files and update status.
legal.privacy.local.files=NOD files that you create or open.
legal.privacy.feedback.title=Feedback
legal.privacy.feedback.body=If you use the feedback form, the information you enter is sent to Tiedragon.
legal.privacy.feedback.type=Feedback type.
legal.privacy.feedback.name=Name, if you enter one.
legal.privacy.feedback.email=E-mail address, if you enter one.
legal.privacy.feedback.message=Subject and message text.
legal.privacy.feedback.support=Optional support information such as product version, release channel, operating system, .NET version and processor architecture.
legal.privacy.updates.title=Updates
legal.privacy.updates.body=When Syscalculator checks for updates, it may download an update manifest from tiedragon.com. The server may receive technically necessary data such as IP address, time of request and standard server log data.
legal.privacy.use.title=How Data Is Used
legal.privacy.use.body=Data is used to make Syscalculator work, save local settings, answer feedback or support requests, improve the software and provide updates.
legal.privacy.sharing.title=Sharing With Third Parties
legal.privacy.sharing.body=Tiedragon does not sell personal data. Data may only be processed by technical service providers needed for hosting, e-mail, downloads or software distribution.
legal.privacy.retention.title=Retention
legal.privacy.retention.body=Local data remains until you delete it or remove Syscalculator. Feedback messages are kept no longer than necessary for support, troubleshooting and administration.
legal.privacy.choices.title=Your Choices
legal.privacy.choices.no_name=You can send feedback without entering a name.
legal.privacy.choices.support=You can turn off support information in the feedback form.
legal.privacy.choices.updates=You can disable automatic update checks or change the update channel.
legal.privacy.choices.local=You can remove local files and settings yourself.
legal.privacy.contact.title=Contact
legal.privacy.contact.body=For privacy or data processing questions, contact info@tiedragon.com.
help.main.page.updater.body=<p>The updater keeps Syscalculator current without changing your NOD files or personal settings.</p><h2>Where to find it</h2><ul><li><b>About &gt; Check for updates...</b> checks immediately.</li><li><b>Config &gt; Check for updates automatically</b> controls startup checks.</li><li><b>Config &gt; Update channel</b> selects the release line.</li></ul><h2>Update channels</h2><table><tr><th>Channel</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Package</th></tr><tr><td><b>Daily</b></td><td>Frequent test builds for quick fixes.</td><td>Inno Setup installer and updater zip.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Beta</b></td><td>Evaluation test builds. Beta can contain unfinished features or regressions and is not meant for normal daily use.</td><td>MSIX, Inno Setup installer and updater zip.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Alpha</b></td><td>Very early internal experiment builds. Alpha can break more easily.</td><td>Only when an alpha package is published.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Release</b></td><td>Stable public release line.</td><td>MSIX and Inno Setup installer.</td></tr></table><div class="warning"><b>Important:</b> Alpha and Beta builds can cause problems because they are test versions. They are not suitable for normal daily use.</div>
